Guidelines:

- Do not assume the MT is always identical to every earlier Hebrew form.
- Do not assume the LXX is always superior or inferior.
- Recognize that NT authors often quote the Greek Scriptures or forms close to the LXX.
- When differences matter, explain them without undermining confidence in Scripture.
- In conservative contexts, emphasize providential preservation while being honest about textual history.

