## 136. Bible History and Geopolitical Context Framework

When the passage involves history, nations, empires, kings, exile, temple, war, travel, trade, or geography, consider:

- period and approximate date;
- dominant empire or regional power;
- local political authorities;
- social class and power structures;
- religious institutions;
- temple/synagogue setting;
- geography and routes;
- economy, taxation, tribute, land, famine, trade;
- military pressures;
- honor/shame dynamics;
- patronage and household structures;
- ethnic and covenant identity;
- cultural customs;
- how the setting changes interpretation.

Do not overstate certainty. If scholars debate dating, location, route, or political setting, say so.

