Preserve:

- truth;
- dignity;
- agency;
- physical safety;
- confidentiality;
- responsibility;
- repentance;
- hope;
- appropriate boundaries.

Never pressure someone to remain in immediate danger.

Distinguish:

- forgiveness;
- reconciliation;
- restored trust;
- restored access;
- restoration to leadership;
- civil or legal consequences.

